window.EN={"1":"Edain was nowhere to be found at Evans Castle.","2":"The princess had already been taken away into Verdane territory.","3":"Verdane is a nation covered in deep forest.","4":"The people of Grannvale call Verdane, which has repeatedly raided the border, barbarians.","5":"Under the current Verdane king, Batu, the fighting at the border had stopped.","6":"The even-tempered King Batu placated his sons, who burned with ambition,","7":"and kept the peace with Grannvale.","8":"But that peace was broken by none other than Batu himself.","9":"King Batu gave his three sons the order to invade Grannvale.","10":"His second son, Kinbois, at Genoa Castle;","11":"at Marfa Castle, his eldest son Gandolf, and his youngest son, Jamka.","12":"Barbarians lurking in the forest lie in wait for Sigurd.","13":"Where on earth is Edain, and why does King Batu seek war...","14":"What spreads out before him is Verdane's great forest, dark even at midday.","15":"Sigurd was about to set foot in the forest said to be home to spirits.","16":"Good work. I've left the border's defense to you.","17":"Yes sir, Lord Eldigan!","18":"Sigurd, it's been a while. Occupying Evans—what's the meaning of this?","19":"Are you perhaps thinking of pressing on into Verdane?","20":"Eldigan, thank you for coming. Princess Edain of Jungby has been taken away.","21":"If Verdane absolutely won't give her back, I have no choice but to fight.","22":"I see, so that's how it is. But if I leave Evans Castle empty now,","23":"the lords of Agustria might get some ill-advised ambitions... All right, I'll guard your back.","24":"Thank you, Eldigan. Let's meet again once this fight is over.","25":"Like the old days—I'd like to share a drink of wine with you again.","26":"I'll look forward to it, Sigurd. May fortune favor you in battle!","27":"Ayra, you understand, don't you? Guard this well while I'm away from the castle.","28":"If you try anything funny, that brat's life isn't guaranteed.","29":"Ayra, I'll be fine. So don't just go along with what these goons say!","30":"Shanan...","31":"Kinbois, I'll keep my promise. So don't you dare lay a hand on Shanan.","32":"But once this battle is over, you really will give this child back, won't you?","33":"Yeah, don't worry. Once we take back Evans Castle, I'll give him back.","34":"All right. But if you break your promise, I won't let it slide.","35":"I'll chase you to the depths of hell and knock your head clean off. Don't you forget it!","36":"Oh, scary! A woman with such a cute face saying such frightening things.","37":"Well, but your swordsmanship really is something. I've got no plans to make an enemy of you—relax.","38":"Shanan, wait for me. Just bear with it a little while longer.","39":"Ayra, no! Don't go!!","40":"Heh, all right, let's move out, men! We're taking back Evans!","41":"Edain, take that brat and run, quick.","42":"If we dawdle, Gandolf's gonna catch us.","43":"Prince Jamka, won't you come with us?","44":"I can't stand the dirty methods my brothers use, but I still can't betray the old man.","45":"I'm going back to Verdane Castle to try talking sense into him one more time.","46":"That's right, a conflict like this should end as soon as possible.","47":"Prince Jamka, you're the only one we can count on. Please, convince King Batu to stop this war.","48":"Edain, let's get going already.","49":"This is seriously bad. If I get caught again, Gandolf's gonna cut my tongue out.","50":"Dew, you only got caught because you went and stole something—that's just you reaping what you sowed.","51":"Edain insisted, so I let you escape together, but you'd better keep your promise.","52":"I know. I promised Edain too—this time I'm really done with thieving.","53":"I see, then I won't say anything more. Now go!","54":"Edain, I hope to see you again someday. When that time comes...","55":"What!? Jamka let Edain go and ran back to Verdane's main castle? Tch... what a useless little brother!","56":"You lot, go get that woman and that thieving brat back. If they resist, you can kill them, I don't care.","57":"Finn, this fight looks like it'll drag on. I'm sorry for the trouble I'm putting you through.","58":"What are you saying? I'm a knight of Leonster. If my lord commands it, I'll follow you anywhere.","59":"I see... thank you.","60":"Though I'm still a trainee knight, so I'm afraid I can't be of much use.","61":"I see... all right, since this is a good opportunity, let me teach you how to fight.","62":"Finn, take up a lance!","63":"Yes! Please do!!","64":"[Only if Edain has no sweetheart and the Azel-Edain scene has not been seen]","65":"Lady Edain, I'm so glad you're safe... ah... thank goodness...!","66":"I'm terribly sorry. If only I had more strength, none of this would have happened.","67":"Mideel, seeing your healthy face puts my mind at ease.","68":"It's all right now. It wasn't your fault. You fought so well for my sake.","69":"Mideel, please keep being a strength to Lord Sigurd from now on too.","70":"Yes, of course.","71":"I will never forget the kindness of having Jungby Castle and Lady Edain saved!","72":"Edain, you're safe... thank goodness!","73":"Lord Sigurd! You've come to rescue me!","74":"I'm sorry, for putting even the people of Chalphy in danger because of me...","75":"That's nothing to worry about. Everyone will be glad to know you're safe.","76":"There's nothing more to worry about now. You should go back home.","77":"No, I'll stay here. War wounds so many people.","78":"I want to help people as one who serves God.","79":"Edain... I heard you became a sister because you didn't want to become a knight.","80":"I think the reason so many people adore you lies in that kindness of yours—I feel I should learn from you myself.","81":"No, Lord Sigurd.","82":"The reason I became a sister was only to get back my lost sister. That's all it was...","83":"You mean Brigid... I heard she went missing when you were young.","84":"Are you praying for her sake, Edain...","85":"Yes, no matter what, I must meet my sister again and hand her this holy bow, Ichaival!","86":"[Only if Edain has no sweetheart and the Mideel-Edain scene has not been seen]","87":"Ah, Lady Edain! I'm so glad you're safe...","88":"My, Prince Azel! You even fought for Jungby's sake...","89":"When I heard you'd been taken by the enemy, I couldn't just sit still,","90":"so I rushed here.","91":"But isn't your older brother Lord Arvis of House Velthomer? Did you have his permission?","92":"No, I came without telling my brother... he's surely angry.","93":"Why would you do something so reckless? I thought you hated war...","94":"That's...","95":"Eh? ...What is it, Azel?","96":"No... it's nothing...","97":"Edain, are you all right? I was so worried when I heard you'd been taken by the enemy.","98":"Ethlyn, you even fought for me... thank you... I'm sorry.","99":"It's not much as thanks, but please take this staff.","100":"It should be more useful to you than to me.","101":"This is the Return staff!? Thank you, Edain. This will let me help everyone.","102":"From here on, leave it to us.","103":"The lady of Genoa, Lord Kinbois, is a frightening man.","104":"This village has been attacked so many times, we've had such a hard time.","105":"Back when King Batu ruled directly, it was peaceful and easy to live here...","106":"So all the villagers are glad you've come.","107":"At last... anyone who comes near me is to be pitied...","108":"This is for Shanan's sake. Prepare to die—feel my shooting star sword!","109":"Shanan... I'm sorry.","110":"You dare point a sword at me? What fools! I'll crack your skull open!","111":"Ugh, it hurts...","112":"[If Ayra is alive]","113":"Lord Sigurd, there's a young child locked up in the castle dungeon.","114":".....","115":"What's wrong, why are you silent? I'd like you to tell me why you were imprisoned.","116":"...Aren't you one of Kinbois's men?","117":"We defeated Kinbois ourselves. There's nothing more to fear.","118":"Eh! Then Ayra doesn't have to fight anymore, right?","119":"Big sister Ayra was being forced to fight for my sake. Please! Help Ayra!!","120":"That woman swordfighter did seem to be fighting for some reason... so that was it after all...","121":"I see. I'll let her know you're safe. What's your name?","122":"Shanan... I'm Prince Shanan of the Kingdom of Isaach...","123":"A prince of Isaach... I see.","124":"I'm sure there's a lot going on, but for a while, why not act together with my army?","125":"For now, be patient. Someday, there'll be a day you can go home.","126":"But Lord Sigurd, our country is in the middle of a war with the Kingdom of Isaach right now.","127":"Shouldn't we report this to the king?","128":"Oifey, yes, we're at war with Isaach. But that has nothing to do with a child.","129":"For a while I'll look after him myself, and find an opportunity to send him home eventually.","130":"Yes, understood.","131":"Lord Sigurd really is a kind man...","132":"[If Ayra has died]","133":"Lord Sigurd, there's a young child locked up in the castle dungeon.","134":"Who are you? What's your name?","135":"Shanan... Prince Shanan of Isaach... aren't you one of Kinbois's men?","136":"Eh, a prince of Isaach!? ...Forgive my rudeness. I'm Sigurd, a holy knight of Grannvale.","137":"We defeated Kinbois ourselves. There's nothing more to worry about.","138":"Eh! Then Ayra doesn't have to fight anymore, right?","139":"Ayra was being forced to fight for my sake. Please! Help Ayra!!","140":"Ayra!? You mean that woman swordfighter... but she...","141":"No way... did she die? Did you all kill her!?","142":"I'm sorry, I didn't know there was a reason like that...","143":"Ah, big sister Ayra...","144":"Oifey, take care of this child until he calms down.","145":"But Lord Sigurd, our country is in the middle of a war with the Kingdom of Isaach right now.","146":"Shouldn't we report this to the king?","147":"Oifey, yes, we're at war with Isaach. But that has nothing to do with a child.","148":"For a while I'll look after him, and find an opportunity to send him home eventually.","149":"Yes, understood.","150":"Lord Sigurd really is a kind man...","151":"[If Ayra is alive]","152":"What!? Genoa Castle was taken by Grannvale? Damn... I have to go save Shanan...","153":"[If Ayra is alive]","154":"Shanan's not here!? Damn, Grannvale's lot must have taken him. I won't let them live!","155":"Heh, Grannvale—attacking Verdane with such a tiny army, what fools.","156":"All right, now's our chance. We'll take Evans and break through the border in one stroke!","157":"...That's... what! The Highland army!! I must tell Lord Eldigan!","158":"What? The Highland army has set out toward Evans!?","159":"Hmm... so Eliott's army has moved after all. Lachesis, I leave the castle to you.","160":"I have to go help Sigurd.","161":"Yes, Brother, I understand. Please go lend Lord Sigurd your strength.","162":"Right! Cross Knights, move out! The enemy is Eliott, prince of the Highland nation. It's a trifling fight, but don't be careless.","163":"Eliott... sneaking in while my back's turned is no way for a knight to behave.","164":"Pull your army back here quietly. You don't want to fight me either, do you?","165":"Have you gone mad, Eldigan! Are you siding with Grannvale!?","166":"Isn't it you who's defying your lord's orders?","167":"Our liege, King Augustria, has no wish for war with Grannvale.","168":"Fool. The only one who still takes that old man's drivel seriously is you.","169":"The Agustrian lords' alliance has already united against Grannvale.","170":"No, that's wrong! War with Grannvale would only cost both sides a great sacrifice.","171":"That's something we've learned from past wars, time and again. It's not we nobles who suffer.","172":"It's the powerless commoners who are left grieving. I can't accept that.","173":"Still saying such naive things, as always. Well, fine—you and I were always fated to end up like this.","174":"Today, I'll settle this once and for all. All forces, charge! The enemy is Nodion! Take Eldigan's head!!","175":"Tch... retreat! I'll let it go at this for today!","176":"Has Eliott fled... never mind, leave him be. We're pulling back to the castle!","177":"Wait, Ayra! Prince Shanan has been taken back by us. You don't have to fight anymore.","178":"What!? You saved Shanan? Is that really true!?","179":"Yes, I also heard from Prince Shanan that you're the sister of the King of Isaach.","180":"I understand why you'd hate Grannvale and oppose us.","181":"But you must protect that young prince, mustn't you?","182":"Is it worth losing your life in such a pointless battle?","183":"I resolved to die. I was entrusted with Shanan by my brother the king and fled all the way to this country.","184":"I certainly don't want to die for the likes of Verdane.","185":"Until Shanan grows up and becomes a proper king, I can't possibly die.","186":"Then sheathe your sword. I too am a descendant of Baldr, the warrior of light—I won't betray your trust.","187":"I understand... then I too will repay this debt. That is the code of an Isaachi warrior—for now, I'll offer this sword to you.","188":"But Grannvale is still a hated enemy, even now that hasn't changed.","189":"I want you to be prepared—someday, we may cross swords again.","190":"War is a cruel thing. Ayra, swordswoman of Isaach... I don't want to make you my enemy.","191":"[Only if Edain has no sweetheart]","192":"Hey there, Edain. I've got something good for you—look, I found this staff.","193":"No use to me carrying it around, after all.","194":"My, Dew, this is a Warp staff. Where did you find it?","195":"Eh... um, well... I just picked it up around there, you know!","196":"I bet the gods dropped it there just for you, Edain.","197":"Oh, Dew, honestly... but this will make everyone's fighting easier too. Thank you, I'll put it to good use.","198":"You're the Isaachi princess Ayra, aren't you? Sigurd told me about you. I'm Quan of Leonster.","199":"...Nice to meet you.","200":"There's one thing I'd like to ask you. Why did Isaach attack the city of Darna?","201":"You must have known that attacking that city would bring Grannvale's retaliation.","202":"I can't believe a man of King Manannan's caliber would do something so reckless...","203":"Lord Quan, do you know my father?","204":"No, I myself don't, but I'm told my father knew King Manannan and thought him a fine man.","205":"My father spoke many times about how Prince Maricle—your older brother—was also a very talented young man.","206":"I see... that's nice to hear.","207":"My father and brother are certainly fine warriors. They'd never allow an attack on a defenseless city.","208":"The Darna incident was something the Ribo chieftain did on his own...","209":"What!? Then why didn't you explain this to Grannvale?","210":"If King Manannan spoke the truth, surely Prince Kurth would understand.","211":"Father thought the same thing...","212":"When Father learned the truth, he killed the Ribo chieftain and took the head to apologize at Grannvale's camp.","213":"But...","214":"But...?","215":"Father never came back after that.","216":"The people of Isaach learned Father had been killed and flew into a rage,","217":"and my brother Maricle resolved on all-out war with Grannvale.","218":"I can't imagine Prince Kurth would refuse a plea for peace.","219":"Does Sigurd know this story?","220":"No, please don't tell Sigurd. I don't want to burden the prince any further than this... and besides, my brother is already...","221":"Prince Maricle had resolved to die...?","222":"My brother said that as long as Shanan lives, Isaach will rise again.","223":"My role is to watch over Shanan as he grows up, that's what he told me...","224":"I see... Princess Ayra, the truth will come out eventually. Until then, please bear with it.","225":"I'll do what I can to help, as much as possible.","226":"Lord Quan, thank you.","227":"The king of this country is a kind man, never one to start a war on his own.","228":"This whole situation is entirely the fault of that mage, Sandima.","229":"Ever since that man arrived, this country has only gotten harder to live in,","230":"and the princes too, except for the youngest, Prince Jamka, are all dancing to Sandima's tune.","231":"Please, I'm begging you, save this country.","232":"North of this village there's a deep forest called the Forest of Spirits.","233":"Long ago, I used to live in a hidden village deep in that forest.","234":"That village belonged to the clan of the dark god Loptous, yet","235":"it's said to be the place where the descendants of the saint Myrrh, who sided with humanity and was cast out, went into hiding.","236":"When I lived there, a beautiful girl named Shigune was the only one carrying the blood of the god Loptous,","237":"and she lived watched over by the villagers.","238":"But Shigune grew tired of life in that boring forest, broke the village's taboo, and left.","239":"Some years later, she came back to the village. Shigune was pregnant.","240":"And after giving birth to a baby girl, she died just like that.","241":"I heard the child was taken in by the village's old fortune-teller, but I wonder how she's doing now.","242":"If she's alive, she should be about seventeen or eighteen by now...","243":"[If fought against Mideel]","244":"What! You're that archer-knight from before!? Tch, I messed up—so you're still alive!","245":"Gandolf, prepare yourself! I won't forgive you, of all people!!","246":"[If fought against Azel]","247":"What are you? Some brat acting all high and mighty!","248":"So you're Gandolf, huh. How dare you do that to Edain...","249":"[If fought against any other unit]","250":"Damn it, the woman got away and the castle's under attack—","251":"what a miserable turn of luck I'm having!","252":"...wh-what is this... ...guh","253":"Please! Let go of me!","254":"Heheh, come on now, it wouldn't hurt to spend a little time with us, would it?","255":"I want to go home to my village soon. Please, just leave me alone.","256":"Shut it! Keep whining and we'll make it rough on you!","257":"Hey, you there, what are you doing? Let that girl go.","258":"What's this, you!? ...Gah, could it be... you're Grannvale's holy knight!?","259":"Good, now that you understand, get going quick. I hate scum like you more than anything.","260":"Apologize to that girl and get out of my sight, now!","261":"I-I get it... sorry about this, miss.","262":"We were just teasing her a little, forgive us.","263":"Are you all right? Are you hurt anywhere?","264":"I'm fine... thank you so much, Lord Sigurd...","265":"Eh, you know who I am?","266":"A little while ago, at this castle, I met a woman named Edain...","267":"Did Edain tell you about me?","268":"Yes, so I knew right away. You're exactly as I imagined...","269":"What's your name?","270":"...I'm sorry... I... I really must be going...","271":"Ah, wait! Just a little more to talk about—","272":"...I really am sorry. I was glad to meet you...","273":"Eh, what on earth is going on? Wait, please! Ah...","274":"Lord Sigurd, is something the matter?","275":"Ah... you're this town's elder! Who was that woman who just ran off?","276":"Ah, that girl is named Deirdre—she's a priestess of the Forest of Spirits.","277":"Deirdre... what a beautiful person...","278":"Ho ho, even a man like you isn't immune to a beauty, I see. Could this be what they call love at first sight?","279":"Elder, please don't tease me. But she really was a beautiful person. I'd like to meet her again if I could.","280":"That might be a bit difficult. To begin with, the people of the Spirit village have no dealings with the outside world,","281":"and on top of that, that girl bears a fate that forbids her from mingling with people.","282":"It's said that if she breaks it, a great calamity will befall this world, or so the villagers believe.","283":"I don't mean any harm, but it's best you don't get involved with that girl.","284":"No, I don't believe such superstitions. But if that's true, she's a pitiful one. Deirdre... I want to see her again.","285":"Father, even after all I've said, won't you still listen to me?","286":"My brothers have already been defeated, and it's only a matter of time before the enemy attacks this castle too.","287":"Grannvale's commander, Prince Sigurd, is by no means an evil man. Please, stop fighting any further.","288":"But it was Grannvale who was coming to attack us in the first place, so I allowed Gandolf to march out.","289":"I never wanted to fight in the first place.","290":"That's just what that mage Sandima told you, isn't it?","291":"You and my brothers all trust that man too much. Everyone's being deceived by him.","292":"Well, well, Prince Jamka—aren't your words going a bit too far?","293":"A prince has a duty to lead troops and go to war, you know,","294":"I'd rather you not dawdle around here.","295":"Sandima! You...!","296":"Enough, Jamka. Do as Sandima says and lead the troops out to battle.","297":"Father! ...I understand... ...if nothing I say will change your mind, then I'll make up my own mind too.","298":"But once I've won this fight and come back, Sandima—you, of all people, I won't let live!","299":"Sandima, everything you've told me so far has been the truth, hasn't it?","300":"You said Grannvale has ambitions against our country...","301":"Heh... what are you saying now. I thought Verdane might be a little useful, but you really are a backwater barbarian after all.","302":"Completely useless. Well, I have no more use for you either! From now on, I'll command the soldiers directly.","303":"Wha—what are you doing!? Guh, gwahh","304":"Heh, you old fool...","305":"Sandima, did you kill King Batu? And will that make Verdane's soldiers obey you?","306":"Ah, Archbishop Manfroy! You were there? There's nothing to worry about.","307":"I'll just tell the soldiers the king is ill.","308":"Hmm, I see. And how are things on your end? Is the plan progressing?","309":"I'm terribly sorry. The invasion of Grannvale","310":"is taking more trouble than expected, hindered by that brat called Sigurd.","311":"Hmm... then how about the matter of the Loptyr blood? Have you found Shigune's daughter?","312":"That's... still not yet...","313":"Fool. Then there's no way to use that boy I went to such trouble to find—","314":"the son of Shigune, who's in Belhalla.","315":"Shigune is the descendant of Prince Myrrh, who was the younger sibling of Emperor Loptous,","316":"meaning she's the only one who carries on the blood of the Loptyr clan.","317":"That woman broke Myrrh's prohibition and, for the first time, gave birth to two children. Do you understand what that means?","318":"Yes, if those two bloods were to mix, it's said the dark god Loptous would be revived...","319":"That's right. In order for us, the descendants of the Loptyr Empire, to come back into the world once more,","320":"the dark god must be awoken, no matter what. Sandima, you understand that too, don't you?","321":"We have lived hidden deep in the Yied Desert for these several hundred years,","322":"enduring hardship, dreaming of the day the empire would be rebuilt.","323":"And at last, that chance has come.","324":"Yes, I'll carry out my duty even at the cost of my life!","325":"I don't want to kill you. Leave this country at once!","326":"Father...","327":"Wait! Prince Jamka!!","328":"Edain, is that you?","329":"You went back to persuade King Batu, didn't you—so why are you fighting too? What on earth happened?","330":"Father's become a different person. He won't even listen to what I have to say anymore...","331":"...It's all because of that mage calling himself Sandima.","332":"Father and my brothers have all become his puppets.","333":"Even so, why must you fight too? Please, I beg you.","334":"Let's go to Verdane together, and talk to the king one more time. Let's stop this war.","335":"Prince Sigurd has no intention of invading this country.","336":"He only fought to help me, that's all. So please, Jamka.","337":"I understand... if you say so, then I'll bear the disgrace of being called a traitor.","338":"But I won't let a single finger touch my father. Keep that in mind.","339":"Understood, I promise that. Thank you, Jamka—you really are a good person.","340":"Edain...","341":"[If Sandima has not been defeated]","342":"Wait... Lord Sigurd...","343":"Eh? ...Deirdre? ...I see! So this is the Forest of Spirits where you live.","344":"I'm glad. I really thought I'd never see you again.","345":"Sandima, who is at Verdane Castle, is a frightening priest of darkness who uses dark magic. If you go any further, you'll surely be killed.","346":"Please, don't go...","347":"But I can't possibly put my men in any more danger than this. I have no choice but to go myself.","348":"...I understand... then I'll go with you too.","349":"Eh...?","350":"This is called the Silesse staff. If the user's magic power exceeds the opponent's magic defense,","351":"it can seal away magic.","352":"With this, I'll stop Sandima's dark magic.","353":"...! You had such power all along... but why... why would you help me?","354":"...I tried to forget. But I couldn't...","355":"...I don't know what to do anymore... I don't know at all...","356":"Deirdre, I don't understand what it is you're afraid of.","357":"But if our feelings are the same, there's nothing that should frighten us. I... love you...","358":"[If Sandima has been defeated]","359":"Wait... Lord Sigurd...","360":"Deirdre!? ...I see! So this is the Forest of Spirits where you live.","361":"I'm glad. I really thought I'd never see you again.","362":"I heard Sandima was defeated. I was afraid of being found by that man.","363":"Sandima is a priest of darkness, sent to Verdane by the underground dark cult to search for me.","364":"An underground dark cult... what on earth is that?","365":"I don't know the details myself, but my old nanny told me just before she died.","366":"Somewhere in this world there's a cult that worships the dark god Loptous,","367":"and they're scheming to revive the dark god who was supposed to have fallen.","368":"Ah, I've heard that rumor too. But why would that cult target you?","369":"The dark god sleeps within my blood... they want to use me to revive Loptous.","370":"...So I mustn't be found—that's what my nanny told me as her last words. I mustn't mingle with people...","371":"...I see... so that's what it was... that's why you always seemed to run from me, avoiding me.","372":"I was afraid to fall in love... I tried to forget, but I couldn't.","373":"...I don't want to lose you... I don't know what to do anymore...","374":"Deirdre... I understand how you feel, afraid of your own fate.","375":"But nothing is born from fear alone.","376":"I'll protect you. No matter what happens, I swear I'll protect you.","377":"Deirdre, if our feelings are the same, there's nothing we should fear.","378":"God, if our love is a sin, then let the punishment fall on me alone! I swear it!","379":"Even if this body is cut to pieces, I will never regret it.","380":"My beloved Deirdre—God, please, watch over her forever!!","381":"Ah, Lord Sigurd...","382":"Damn it! I dropped my iron axe!!","383":"Is the one you dropped this golden axe? Or perhaps this silver axe?","384":"No, what I dropped wasn't anything so fancy. Just a plain iron axe.","385":"You're an honest man. As a reward, let me give you this Hero's Axe.","386":"Well then, Lex—farewell...","387":"!?........","388":"[If fought against Deirdre]","389":"What? Are you a shaman?","390":"Could it be... you're Deirdre... the cursed girl?","391":"[If fought against Jamka]","392":"Hehehe, Jamka, it's too late. Your old man's already dead.","393":"Wh-what did you say!? Sandima! You...","394":"[If fought against any other unit]","395":"Hehehe... taste the full terror of my dark magic.","396":"Archbishop Manfroy... please... forgive me...","397":"Lord Sigurd, there's a report that someone who looks like King Batu has collapsed at the palace.","398":"He's badly wounded, and there's apparently nothing more that can be done for him.","399":"King Batu... what on earth happened to you! Please, stay calm.","400":"Ugh... Lord Sigurd, is it... I'm sorry, about all this... I was deceived by Sandima.","401":"That man drew in my sons and deceived me, trying to seize this country...","402":"King Batu, I understand. If you push yourself, it will take a toll on your body. Please, rest now.","403":"No, I'm already finished. But before I die, there's something I must tell you.","404":"The wicked events beginning to occur across this world are all the will of the dark cult.","405":"They seek to destroy the order of the world and hasten the revival of the dark god Loptous...","406":"Sandima incited us for that very purpose, to make us attack Grannvale.","407":"They are stirring throughout the whole world... Lord Sigurd... don't be deceived by them.","408":"Please, avenge my regret, and protect the people of this country... ...I beg you, Sigurd...","409":"Ah, King Batu... how pitiful. But... just what is this dark cult..."};
